ROLE: systems_reviewer  VOTE: red
PROMPT_VERSION: v001
EXISTING_IMPLEMENTATIONS: [
  {system: "SGLang Adaptive Speculative Decoding", url: "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/docs/advanced_features/adaptive_speculative_decoding.md", overlap: "Direct: adjusts speculative_num_steps/speculative_num_draft_tokens at runtime using EMA of accepted draft length, prebuilt runtime states, hysteresis, and tier switching for workloads whose accept length changes over time."},
  {system: "Hugging Face Transformers Dynamic Speculation", url: "https://huggingface.co/blog/dynamic_speculation_lookahead", overlap: "Direct prior mechanism: dynamic speculation lookahead / assistant token schedule adjusts draft length during generation; arXiv 2405.04304 reports DISCO dynamic SL vs best static SL."},
  {system: "vLLM Speculative Decoding", url: "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/main/docs/features/speculative_decoding/README.md", overlap: "Ships speculative decoding methods including draft-model, EAGLE, MTP, N-gram, suffix decoding, and custom proposers; suffix decoding uses dynamic speculation depth with num_speculative_tokens as a maximum."},
  {system: "TensorRT-LLM Speculative Decoding", url: "https://github.com/NVIDIA/TensorRT-LLM/blob/main/docs/source/features/speculative-decoding.md", overlap: "Ships draft/target, EAGLE 3, NGram, MTP, PARD, DFlash, suffix automaton, and user-provided drafting; includes dynamic tree mode but not the specific session-phase detector."},
  {system: "FlashInfer", url: "https://github.com/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer", overlap: "Kernel support for chain speculative sampling; implementation substrate, not a session-phase adaptive policy."},
  {system: "LMCache", url: "https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache", overlap: "KV-cache reuse/offload integration with vLLM; no direct adaptive speculative draft-length policy found."}
]
CONTRIBUTION_TYPE: insight
SCALE_REALISM: Does not hold as a positive systems claim at realistic workload. The L0 artifact is reproducible enough for an analytic negative: preregistered, CPU/std-lib script, full 3,024-row sweep, summary JSON. But it is not a realistic systems artifact: no real draft/target model pair, no GPU server, no real long agentic traces, no measured phase detector, no measured CUDA graph/switching/recompile cost. Under the packet's modeled realistic point, best-tuned fixed captures 92.7% median of adaptive gain and adaptive loses -2.22% mean net tok/s with overhead.
RATIONALE: A shipping system already implements the core adaptive speculative-decoding mechanism: SGLang runtime-adapts speculative steps/draft tokens from observed accept lengths, explicitly for accept-length changes over time. HF Transformers and DISCO independently cover dynamic speculation lookahead. Therefore the adaptive draft-length mechanism is not a systems design contribution. The only surviving contribution is the negative analytic insight that session-phase drift still collapses against a best-tuned fixed k because throughput-vs-k has broad overlapping plateaus. That insight is supported by the packet's own numbers, but it is L0 only and should not be promoted as a real-scale systems result without real traces and GPU measurements.
